  <data name="AdminRequiredInfoBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Administrator required</value></data>
  <data name="AdminRequiredInfoBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>Changing this startup item requires an administrator. Restart BECETTI SECURITY as administrator from Settings.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleStartup.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Startup Manager</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleStartup.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real registry startup entries — the same Run-key and Task Manager convention Windows itself uses. No performance impact score is invented: Windows does not expose one through any stable API.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleSoftware.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Software Manager</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleSoftware.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real installed applications from the Windows registry — the same list Settings &gt; Apps shows. Uninstalling only launches the application's own real uninstaller; nothing is removed directly.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleDrivers.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Driver Monitor</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleDrivers.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Real installed device drivers from Windows (WMI), the same inventory Device Manager uses. BECETTI SECURITY has no driver issue database of its own — check Windows Update or the manufacturer's site for updates.</value></data>

  <data name="TitleEmergency.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Emergency Center</value></data>
  <data name="SubtitleEmergency.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A single place for 'something feels wrong' moments — real status, quick access to Windows' own tools, and BECETTI AI for help.</value></data>
